('Grocery prices are up over 25% since 2020; car insurance up about 50% in 4 years; hospital services up 6.7% last year, the most since 2010.','Grocery prices are up over\n25% cumulatively since 2020','Directionally '+R+' (CPI food at home and motor vehicle insurance indexes). Exact base months and the 6.7% hospital figure not checked. '+U,[]),
('A family of four spends $1,300-$1,430 a month on food, versus about $800 in 2020 for the same cart.','The average family of four now spends between $1,300','The $1,300-$1,430 range resembles USDA food-plan costs; the $800 2020 baseline implies a ~70% rise, inconsistent with the video\'s own "over 25%" grocery figure. Internally inconsistent; '+U,[]),
