('The September 2025 BLS benchmark revision found 911,000 fewer jobs as of March 2025; "about 10% smaller".','911,000\nfewer jobs','The preliminary -911,000 benchmark (9 Sep 2025) is '+R+'. "About 10% smaller" is WRONG: 911,000 is about 0.6% of ~159 million payroll jobs. It may be a garbled reference to job growth over the period.',[]),
('2025 announced layoffs 1,206,374, up 58%, highest since COVID; hiring plans 507,647, lowest since 2010.','total announced layoffs hit 1,206,374','CGC: Challenger year-end 2025 report (8 Jan 2026) confirms the lowest YTD hiring since 2010 and 54,836 AI-cited cuts. The exact 1,206,374 and 507,647 totals were not seen in the summaries.',['CGC']),
('AI cited in 54,836 cuts in 2025; by March 2026 AI was the leading stated reason, 15,341 in one month, 25% of cuts.','54,836\njob cuts explicitly cited AI','CGC verified for 54,836 (2025). DOGE actions, not AI, were the leading 2025 reason. The March 2026 figures are not checked. '+U,['CGC']),
