('Fidelity: a 65-year-old couple needs $345,000 for medical costs; one in three adults has zero retirement savings.','Fidelity estimates a 65-year-old couple','Fidelity 2025 estimate ($172,500 per person) '+R+'. The one-in-three figure is not checked.',[]),
('Saving 10% of $63,000 ($6,300) + 3% match at 7% for 30 years gives ~$830,000; $342,000 real at 3% inflation; 3.7% gives $12,654; plus $23,700 Social Security = $36,354.','contribute 10% of the\nmedian household income, about $63,000','K02: monthly contributions of (6,300+1,890)/12 at 7% for 30 years give $832,630. 830,000/1.03^30 = $341,949; x3.7% = $12,652; +23,700 = $36,352. Reproduces. The "$63,000 median household income" contradicts the video\'s own $83,730. MSWR: Morningstar raised its safe rate to 3.9% for 2026 in December 2025, so 3.7% was STALE at the April 2026 upload.',['MSWR']),
