('The 401(k) began in the Revenue Act of 1978 as a way for executives to defer income.','Revenue Act of\n1978','Section 401(k) was enacted by the Revenue Act of 1978 ('+R+'). "Tax loophole for executives" is interpretive framing.',[]),
('Austin couple: $450,000 home, 10% down, 7%: $2,990 payment; total $4,165, $2,265 above rent, 47% of $8,900 take-home.','their mortgage payment at\n7% interest would be roughly $2,990','K02: P&I on $405,000 at 7%/30y = $2,694. $2,990 only holds with ~$300 PMI, which is not mentioned. Sum 2,990+520+280+375 = $4,165; 4,165-1,900 = $2,265; 4,165/8,900 = 46.8% (reproduce).',[]),
('NAHB (March 2025): 74.9% of households (100.6 million) cannot afford a median-priced new home; required income $112,000-$141,000.','74.9%\nof US households','NAHB verified: 2025 priced-out estimate 100.6M of 141.1M households (74.9%); income needed $141,366 at 6.5%. The $112,000 lower bound is not checked. K02 gap vs $83,730: $28,270-$57,270 (video "$30,000 to $57,000", approximately).',['NAHB']),
