('Bankrate: renting beats buying in all 50 largest metros; San Jose renters save $4,783/month; in 2015 the gap was 84 cents.','renting is financially better than\nbuying in all 50','Bankrate 2025 rent-vs-buy study '+R+'. The specific values are not checked. '+U,[]),
('Median first-time buyer age hit 40; first-time share 21%, lowest since 1981.','The median first-time\nhomebuyer age just hit 40','NAR 2025 Profile (Nov 2025) values '+R+' (age 40; share 21%, record low).',[]),
('Goldman went from 15% recession odds in Jan 2025 to 65% by April, then 30%; JPMorgan peaked at 65%.','Goldman Sachs went from\n15% recession probability','GSR: Goldman raised 12-month odds to 45% (6-7 Apr 2025); a 65% call on 9 Apr was withdrawn to 45% the same day after the tariff pause. JPMorgan\'s published peak was 60%. "65%" overstates both. PARTLY WRONG.',['GSR']),
('In 2008 federal debt was 64% of GDP with 525 bp of Fed room; 2020 stimulus over $5T; today debt ~100% of GDP, interest over $1T, deficit $1.7T.','our federal\ndebt sat at 64% of GDP','Fed funds were 5.25% in 2007 (525 bp, '+R+'). The 64% matches gross federal debt in FY2007-08 (held-by-public was ~39%). The debt, interest and deficit levels are broadly '+R+'.',[]),
